"F-fine, go, then!
Just try not to come crawling back
with your tail between your legs!"{w}

"Blubbering?
Why would I ever blubber over you, Soara... As if!
I-I don't even get what you're saying!"{w}

"I am Rondelgius.{w}Sovereign of dragons -- in other words, the Dragon Lord!"{w}{p}"I hear you lot are rather capable.{w}...However!{w}Can you overcome MY trials?"{w}{p}"Come! If you wish to grow even stronger,
then take up my trials!"{w}{p}"You can do it!
I know you can do it!!"{w}

"That's the spirit!{w}Then here is the first trial!{w}The trial ground is... the Flotban Snowfield!!"{w}{p}"Flotban is a land of bitter cold.{w}Without protection against the cold,
you'll freeze just walking around!"{w}{p}"Bring me back the Ice Strawberries
that are said to grow there!!"{w}

"Now, I shall hand down the next trial!{w}The next trial ground is... Heerdahl!!"{w}{p}"They say an unknown apparition appears
in a bunker on the golf course there!{w}Challenge that apparition and beat it!"{w}{p}"Now go, adventurers!{w}Your hot blood, your very soul!
Let them come bursting out!!"{w}{p}"I shall await your return here.{w}I pray for your success."{w}

"Magnificent!{w}Your power is nothing ordinary!!"{w}{p}"The anomaly in that place
will surely never occur again!!"{w}{p}"I have no grounds for it,
but I am certain of it!!"{w}

"But still,
this Dragon Centaur V or whatever --
just who could it be, I wonder?"{w}

"Come on, come on, any song requests?{w}Classics, folk songs, nursery rhymes --
Haleorat here will play them for you!"{w}{p}"A song from your hometown, that old tune you miss,
whatever you like!"{w}

"Nope, old man. Get lost."{w}{p}"New songs are nice too, but old songs
are packed with the feelings of the people who came before.
Man, the romance of it!"{w}

"Wait, but... Hm?{w}That's weird... what language is this?{w}It isn't Spirit Script either... I can't read this."{w}{p}"Maybe this sheet music was written
long, long before we'd ever imagine."{w}{p}"Even the oldest folk songs I know
don't use letters or words like these.{w}Isn't there anyone who could decipher it..."{w}

"No, no, no, wait just a MOMENT!!"{w}{p}"Whyyy is some lowly huuuman heeere~~!!
Do not paraaade your vulgar face
before meee~! Begone!!"{w}

"I bought an old painting from a peddler, you see.
It is called the Forsaken Painting 'Morning of Ruin'."{w}{p}"An ominous name, is it not?{w}I wanted to know what sort of history lies behind it."{w}{p}"I have had all manner of people look into it...{w}and in that painting were the very same letters as these."{w}{p}" ┤┯├┌┷ ┗┫┷┴├┯ ┿┯┿┳┌

   That is what it says. Rather similar, wouldn't you say?"{w}

"...???{w}The 'friends' in this song... those are the Four Sages of the Land, right?"{w}{p}"Let's see, Raizam the Earth Sage, Omshokopo the Wind Sage, Radrecht the Fire Sage, and Shirinmorin the Water Sage... was it?"{w}{p}"Weren't the Four Sages born together with the Earth Goddess -- I mean, Lady Fiona?"{w}{p}"...If so, then who's Urna?{w}None of the folk songs or old tales I know has anyone named Urna in it..."{w}{p}"......"{w}{p}"Something about... this song is bad news.{w}It's just my gut talking, but...
I've got a feeling spreading these lyrics around would be bad news."{w}{p}"...Huh?
The old goblin told you not to sing it, too?{w}I knew it..."{w}{p}"All right, then I'll give up on this song.{w}I'll keep it sealed away inside me."{w}

"Whaaat are you, you lowly huuuman!!
Do not paraaade your vulgar face
before meee~! Begone!!"{w}

"Hm, a face I have not seen before. An adventurer?{w}Oh? Then allow me to introduce myself.
I am Volms. A collector of antiquities."{w}{p}"Should you come by any rare articles, bring them to me.
Depending on the piece, I may buy it at a good price."{w}

"Listen to this, customer.{w}Lunea's working really hard, you know.
But no proper customers ever come!"{w}{p}"Just the other day,
this weird kid came over from Semnadoc~"{w}

"Non, non~
I mean a shop on the cutting edge of fashion.
Like, this year's trends."{w}

"That kid's name was Caron,{w}and after that, I got nagged about all sorts of things,
like the shop's decor and how I lay out the goods..."{w}{p}"If I stock even more amazing tentacles and fangs,
maybe I won't get any more complaints?{w}For now, I've got to get some goods to sell..."{w}

"I found work at Walmitt's plaaace!
Cuttin' down treeees!
Splittin' firewood and gettin' split myseeelf..."{w}

"Hm? 'Bahamut on a Single Line'?"{w}{p}"...Oh-ho,
so a request like that came in at Walmitt's?{w}I see, I see..."{w}{p}"You may not believe this, but when I was young,
with a Flame Rod and Airy Vider Meat for bait..."{w}

"Wh-what's there to complain about!?"{w}{p}"Fine, then how about I grant you a wish or something?
{11:0001:0017}~, and all that!
Wahah, wahah!!"{w}

"Wait, hear me out to the end!!{w}...It's a tempting offer, sure,
but don't you think this reward is odd?"{w}{p}"It's far too generous for just recruiting a fighter.{w}You can bet a request like this is almost certainly dirty.
'Dirty' -- you know what that means, right?"{w}

"No matter how much money is in it,
I can't take on a request that dangerous."{w}{p}"So it's void.
I'm planning to tear up the request form, too."{w}

"You people sure are persistent.{w}All right, if you insist that much,
let's make a trade."{w}{p}"Complete three of the requests I'm holding,
and I might just hand it over as a special favor."{w}{p}"Well? Not a bad deal, is it?{w}Got it? Then get to it, and be quick about it!!"{w}

"Chomp...
Mmmmm!! Thoooo yummyyy!!"{w}{p}"After you've done thith much for me,
Jeratan hath to pitch in too!{w}I'll give you the betht treatment ever!!"{w}

"Oh, this?
It's a card of you, Lord Mersenne."{w}{p}"They were selling them at the souvenir shop over there,
and I just couldn't help buying one!"{w}

"There is no need to go so far as taking
that grueling exam to work at the Cathedral.
If you come to pray, you can see me like anyone else."{w}

"Sorry, but I can't give you the answer.{w}You have to face your own heart
and decide for yourself."{w}{p}"If times weren't what they are, I'd tell you
to go stand under Moonlight Falls.{w}Nothing beats a waterfall for training the spirit, you know."{w}

"Yes!"{w}{p}"I admired you so much, Lord Mersenne,
that I lost sight of the real reason
I came to Semnadoc!"{w}

"Because you realized this,
you have taken your first true step
as a member of the clergy, here and now!!"{w}

{0E}"Semnadoc is number one.{0F}
But number two is Lord Mersenne!
Ehehe~"{w}

"Welcome!{w}Welcome to the Caron Main Store,
run by Caron!!"{w}{p}"Huh? You can't find a Caron Branch?{w}Ugh, quit nagging. That's still to come!"{w}{p}"From here on, I'm going to spread my brand
and open stores in all sorts of cities!!{w}So you'd better buy plenty too, customer!!"{w}

"Really? I'm counting on you, okay? What I'm about to tell you
is a line of business that surely nobody
on this continent has ever tried."{w}

"But when I took the idea to them,
they told me, 'We cannot stock them
unless their practicality is proven.'"{w}

"And this proof of practicality? They said it means
wearing Caron brand goods and fighting
that school's teachers -- and winning!"{w}

"It's not much of a thank-you, but
I'll let you lot buy
Caron brand goods cheap."{w}{p}"I've marked them down, so buy some before you go."{w}

"Here at this Cathedral, for any worshippers who wish it,
we offer a variety of talks about the gods,
though they run a little long."{w}

"This town has nothing but religion,
but I'm sure one stroll around it will leave you
feeling refreshed!"{w}

"Do my oracles... come true?{w}Haha, forgive me for asking something so odd."{w}{p}"I have been put on a pedestal as the foremost figure
of the Semnadoc faith, but..."{w}{p}"Not one archbishop in history
has ever heard Semnadoc's voice directly."{w}

"They say Semnadoc is not only
the god of space but also the god of laughter."{w}{p}"I'm not joking around, you know.{w}A life without smiles
would be sad, wouldn't it?"{w}

"My, my,
some cute little lambs
have wandered in."{w}{p}"What shall I do?{w}Maybe I'll just send you right back..."{w}{p}"Hmmm..."{w}{p}"......"{w}{p}{0E}"......{0F}Oh well, never mind."{w}{p}"This is Elminage.{w}And I am Hisbert. Nice to meet you."{w}

"Ah, now I remember."{w}{p}"New Land 304972... Orses and Sarijana,
who were trying to relocate life there..."{w}{p}"...forcibly fused it with Urna, the unregistered land.{w}They even revised its system so that life could survive there."{w}{p}"As a result, this land became control number 304972,
of the Rade 301 system."{w}

"Honestly, what a pain they caused.{w}They were even so considerate as to change
the land's name to Fiur Rade."{w}{p}"Did they really think something like that
could fool the eyes of the System?"{w}

...Why was that? Despite the words she spat out,
Hisbert's expression seemed fond, as if she were
reminiscing about days long past.{w}

"No way, even the system's the same: 301!"{w}{p}"Back then... that was when Void, god of space,
became chief god, and the plans for creating the Eld
were overhauled across the board."{w}

